{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1094 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b0bc279d337d725321d9f8a1dd6d0249a2d5f993d5ed147dec85bbe87f8edeb3" :edb/db-before-t 1093 :edb/db-after-t 1094 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534406 50 #inst "2026-10-07T00:47:14.309Z" 13194139534406 true] [17592186078306 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286679 13194139534406 true] [17592186078306 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286683 13194139534406 true] [17592186078306 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286693 13194139534406 true] [17592186078307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286676 13194139534406 true] [17592186078307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286686 13194139534406 true] [17592186286676 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286677 13194139534406 true] [17592186286676 1089 "q-313361" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286676 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534406 true] [17592186286676 1100 "In an acoustics lab, the ambient noise power (in decibels) at frequency $f$ (in $\\text{kHz}$) is modeled by the function\n\n$$\nN(f)={2}^{-2{f}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the exact value of the instantaneous rate at which the noise power is changing with respect to frequency when $f=2\\,\\text{kHz}?$ \n\nThe instantaneous rate of change when $f=2\\,\\text{kHz}$ is \n{{field-1}} decibels per $\\text{kHz}.$" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286676 1113 #uuid "f9917547-0ce3-572e-9107-f7432717d826" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286676 1145 "The instantaneous rate of change at which the ambient noise power is changing when $f=2$ kHz is equal to ${N}^{′}(2).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $N(f)$ with respect to $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}^{′}(f) & =\\frac{d}{df}({2}^{-2{f}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={2}^{-2{f}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot (-4f) \\\\  & =-4f\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\,{2}^{-2{f}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $f=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}^{′}(2) & =-4(2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\,{2}^{-2(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\,{2}^{-8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{256} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the ambient noise power is changing when $f=2\\,\\text{kHz}$ is $-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{32}$ decibels per $\\text{kHz}.$" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286678 13194139534406 true] [17592186286677 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534406 true] [17592186286677 1041 "field-1" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286677 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286678 13194139534406 true] [17592186286677 1110 #uuid "0edc23b7-e1b0-5927-8c0c-ddbb598f1b93" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286678 1034 "-\\frac{\\ln(2)}{32}" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286678 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286678 1111 #uuid "aec8549f-1e68-57d4-b394-78228236e0e5" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286679 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286680 13194139534406 true] [17592186286679 1089 "q-313364" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286679 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534406 true] [17592186286679 1100 "The volume of a right square pyramid is increasing. Given that its height $h$ is always twice the length of a base, find the rate of change of the volume of the pyramid with respect to its base length $s.$\n\n*Hint*: The volume of a right square pyramid is $V=\\frac{1}{3}{s}^{2}h.$ \n\nThe rate of change of the pyramid’s volume with respect to $s$ is \n{{field-1}}." 13194139534406 true] [17592186286679 1113 #uuid "ef0e7ebd-8eb3-5e6b-8197-77c0558d373a" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286679 1145 "We are given that $h=2s,$ so we can express the volume of the pyramid $V$ as a function of the base edge length $s$ by substituting $h=2s$ in the formula of the volume. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}{s}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{s}^{2}(2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $V(s)$ with respect to $s$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{d}{ds}\\,(\\frac{2}{3}{s}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{d}{ds}\\,({s}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{s}^{2} \\\\  & =2{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the rate of change of the pyramid’s volume with respect to its base length $s$ is $2{s}^{2}.$" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286680 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286681 13194139534406 true] [17592186286680 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286682 13194139534406 true] [17592186286680 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534406 true] [17592186286680 1041 "field-1" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286680 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286681 13194139534406 true] [17592186286680 1110 #uuid "a76f6768-6175-5831-9bef-cf3c3433a53d" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286681 1034 "2s^2" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286681 1111 #uuid "7874d3c1-1e7d-5935-918f-98a39cbf1ad9" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286682 1034 "6s^2" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286682 1111 #uuid "15d53ce7-5bf9-5cbc-801d-aca9e585a89b" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286683 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286684 13194139534406 true] [17592186286683 1089 "q-341062" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286683 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534406 true] [17592186286683 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004055/assets/34966965452968c2f186efcfbec70591eded02e926eaaac8b90409381b2c8da8.png)\n\nThe area of an equilateral triangle is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the area of the equilateral triangle is increasing with respect to its side length at the moment when its side length is equal to $s=4\\,\\text{in}.$  \n\n*Hint*: The area of an equilateral triangle is $A=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}{s}^{2}.$ \n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at the moment when its side length is $4$ inches is equal to\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286683 1113 #uuid "9d592472-9003-5b10-a17c-3387b33b74c4" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286683 1145 "We know that the area of the equilateral triangle with side $s$ is given by  \n\n$$\nA=A(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}{s}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(s)$  with respect to $s$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}{s}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\cdot (2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}s,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=4$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(4)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 4=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at the moment when the length of the side is $s=4\\,\\text{in}$ is $2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286685 13194139534406 true] [17592186286684 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534406 true] [17592186286684 1041 "field-1" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286684 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286685 13194139534406 true] [17592186286684 1110 #uuid "8ca5d40c-9e54-5ddc-b3c2-854c372680ad" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286685 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286685 1111 #uuid "0297e020-3a86-50b7-9386-a483d810a066" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286686 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286687 13194139534406 true] [17592186286686 1089 "q-48701" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286686 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534406 true] [17592186286686 1100 "The distance $d$, in meters, that a car has traveled after $t$ seconds can be modeled by the function $d(t)=\\frac{2{t}^{3}+7t}{t+1}.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the distance traveled when $t=2$ seconds?" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286686 1113 #uuid "a3049570-7c93-5933-b115-32fd9040b96a" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286686 1145 "The instantaneous rate of change of the distance traveled when $t=2$ seconds is equal to ${d}^{′}(2).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2{t}^{3}+7t}{t+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(6{t}^{2}+7)(t+1)-(2{t}^{3}+7t)(1)}{(t+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}+7}{(t+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{4(2)^{3}+6(2)^{2}+7}{((2)+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32+24+7}{9} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the distance traveled when $t=2$ seconds is $7$ meters per second." 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286688 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286689 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286690 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286691 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286692 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1041 "selection" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286688 13194139534406 true] [17592186286687 1110 #uuid "eb23e50b-47f4-5407-9040-bf5dfa59e78c" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286688 1034 "$7$ meters per second" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534406 true] [17592186286688 1111 #uuid "a30b31a4-56d4-5d23-a5f8-9db9b68d7c4e" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286689 1034 "$5$ meters per second" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534406 true] [17592186286689 1111 #uuid "ac55b287-d233-548f-b85f-3fcfa08faaf8" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286690 1034 "$15$ meters per second" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534406 true] [17592186286690 1111 #uuid "b7aff8bf-20d8-5fcb-aa5b-e8e7ab6cefb8" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286691 1034 "$12$ meters per second" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534406 true] [17592186286691 1111 #uuid "05037bec-ce8d-535f-902e-b7a19174950b" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286692 1034 "$8$ meters per second" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534406 true] [17592186286692 1111 #uuid "267e40a0-b7ee-5c5f-9b62-a2eadd114f3e" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286693 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286694 13194139534406 true] [17592186286693 1089 "q-48722" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286693 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534406 true] [17592186286693 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004055/assets/4915dc00f10fa5edc911cf9744e99e662b705898b32f16391805c7733b8f89e5.png)\n\nThe surface area $A$ of the sphere above is increasing. The radius of the sphere is $r.$ Find the rate of change of the surface area of a sphere with respect to its radius." 13194139534406 true] [17592186286693 1113 #uuid "8ee25135-641c-52e9-bf00-6ce2f154bccb" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286693 1145 "The area of the surface area of the sphere is given by  \n\n$$\nA=A(r)=4\\pi {r}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(r)$ with respect to its radius $r$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi (2r) \\\\  & =8\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286695 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286696 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286697 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286698 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286699 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1041 "selection" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286699 13194139534406 true] [17592186286694 1110 #uuid "0f2ef6e1-9039-5c7a-8032-5209d199c089" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286695 1034 "4\\pi " 13194139534406 true] [17592186286695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286695 1111 #uuid "430855ca-45a4-57ff-b5ec-11aa28304a93" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286696 1034 "\\frac{4r}{\\pi }" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286696 1111 #uuid "5317bac5-b1c9-5af8-ae6d-362e3e413784" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286697 1034 "6r" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286697 1111 #uuid "83b8fe39-d9ce-5246-aaab-db83d6bc72e1" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286698 1034 "10\\pi r" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286698 1111 #uuid "d7a60a95-5eb1-5746-8115-f42608d0b911" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286699 1034 "8\\pi r" 13194139534406 true] [17592186286699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534406 true] [17592186286699 1111 #uuid "b8e50281-f839-5cc6-8fa0-97c616e78072" 13194139534406 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-313361" 17592186286676 "q-313361/field-1" 17592186286677 "q-313361/field-1/eb804d28f6e48656a119bbea626f9c05c81c8a4fa2248b73cd7104ff69717270" 17592186286678 "q-313364" 17592186286679 "q-313364/field-1" 17592186286680 "q-313364/field-1/049ebfb283bb55f03ce63049d9f211259697ab2ec96ea24b01caf42dd8d7a2ef" 17592186286681 "q-313364/field-1/5b039eb22c2d368e423e7973f61fb73a004df68cba3bc4fa13b81a38f48a05e4" 17592186286682 "q-341062" 17592186286683 "q-341062/field-1" 17592186286684 "q-341062/field-1/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" 17592186286685 "q-48701" 17592186286686 "q-48701/selection" 17592186286687 "q-48701/selection/533783b3d8b43c90191079fdd53b7b436b95071b3dcc9310bbb71c8077d17ed2" 17592186286688 "q-48701/selection/8f94bb4b240324b0991e3db4874f14f0b26102c94ea631327925a9767a8dd91c" 17592186286689 "q-48701/selection/974a0be67e0cf3918e9c7444d867bd360890eacc79c1e2533239a7de665b62d9" 17592186286690 "q-48701/selection/b57305573e8687cd1e56a024aa0d19393378c873281af77761a6cc1abaa3bd9c" 17592186286691 "q-48701/selection/d6f9b92e5574bc845d958fa3916c9b77ed0adbd976a1a7e16194566945aa8b9b" 17592186286692 "q-48722" 17592186286693 "q-48722/selection" 17592186286